-- title:
--   Regular local rings are Cohen–Macaulay
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is Noetherian and satisfies `IsRegularLocalRing`, so in particular $R$ is local with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_R$. The assertion is that the depth of $R$ as a module over itself coincides with its Krull dimension, the equality being stated in $\mathrm{WithBot}\ \mathbb{N}^\infty$ after coercing the depth along $\mathbb{N}^\infty \to \mathrm{WithBot}\ \mathbb{N}^\infty$, so that it may be compared with `ringKrullDim R`, which takes values in $\mathrm{WithBot}\ \mathbb{N}^\infty$ in order to accommodate the zero ring. Here [`Module.depth R R`](def/Patching_SystemTypes.html#L34) is the element of $\mathbb{N}^\infty$ given by the supremum of the lengths of those finite lists $s$ of elements of $R$ all of whose entries lie in $\mathfrak{m}_R$ and which form a weakly regular sequence on $R$ in the sense of Mathlib's `Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular`, i.e. each successive entry acts as a non-zerodivisor on the quotient of $R$ by the ideal generated by the preceding entries.
--
--   This is the Cohen–Macaulay property of regular local rings in the form 'depth equals dimension', the depth being computed with respect to the maximal ideal and the module being the ring itself. It is used in the project's treatment of regular local rings, for instance in the proof that a regular local ring is a unique factorisation domain and in the local-dimension arguments behind extension of the relative group law on Jacobians of good reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_depth_self_eq_ringKrullDim.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Patching_SystemTypes

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open IsLocalRing RingTheory

theorem IsRegularLocalRing.depth_self_eq_ringKrullDim
    (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsRegularLocalRing R] :
    (Module.depth R R : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim R := by sorry
